Mirror PR #4733's headersSent guard into ServerResponseService.

Upstream PR #4733 (merged 2025-09-30, present in dspace-9.2) added
`if (res.headersSent) return;` to server.ts but missed
ServerResponseService, which has the same race — observables inside
the SSR chain (Signposting, status setters) keep calling
setHeader/setStatus after BitstreamDownloadPage has already flushed a
302 response, producing ERR_HTTP_HEADERS_SENT stack traces in logs.

Lifecycle: delete this file when upstream merges an equivalent guard
into ServerResponseService. The `patch --fuzz=0` invocation in
deployAngularAssets.sh will fail loudly ("Reversed (or previously
applied) patch detected") once the upstream code already includes the
guard, surfacing the redundancy in the next Docker build.

Refs:
  - https://github.com/DSpace/dspace-angular/issues/2315
  - https://github.com/DSpace/dspace-angular/pull/4733

--- a/src/app/core/services/server-response.service.ts
+++ b/src/app/core/services/server-response.service.ts
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@ export class ServerResponseService {
    * @param message
    */
   setStatus(code: number, message?: string): this {
-    if (this.response) {
+    if (this.response && !this.response.headersSent) {
       this.response.statusCode = code;
       if (message) {
         this.response.statusMessage = message;
@@ -77,7 +77,7 @@ export class ServerResponseService {
    * @param content
    */
   setHeader(header: string, content: string) {
-    if (this.response) {
+    if (this.response && !this.response.headersSent) {
       this.response.setHeader(header, content);
     }
   }
